{
  "title": "Stage 4: Verifying chains and reporting errors",
  "summary": "Build chains with X509Chain against your own roots, at any date, and explain why they fail.",
  "minutes": 18,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "Briefing: `openssl verify`, built in",
      "body": [
        "A CA that can't check its own work is a liability. Add three commands:",
        "",
        "- `verify NAME [at YYYY-MM-DD]` builds the chain with **your roots as the only trust anchors** (default date 2030-06-01). Leaves are checked for serverAuth.",
        "- `distrust ROOTNAME` removes a root from the trust store (it stays available to chain to, so the failure is `UntrustedRoot`).",
        "- `match NAME HOST` checks a host against the SAN only (no CN fallback), like a browser.",
        "",
        "```text",
        "> root Dojo Root",
        "> intermediate Issuing CA",
        "> issue shop.example www.shop.example",
        "> verify shop.example",
        "> verify shop.example at 2032-01-01",
        "> match shop.example api.shop.example",
        "> distrust Dojo Root",
        "> verify shop.example",
        "created root CN=Dojo Root (2030-01-01 to 2050-01-01)",
        "created intermediate CN=Issuing CA under CN=Dojo Root (2030-01-01 to 2040-01-01)",
        "issued CN=shop.example by CN=Issuing CA (2030-01-01 to 2031-01-01) for shop.example, www.shop.example",
        "verify shop.example: OK",
        "  CN=shop.example",
        "  CN=Issuing CA",
        "  CN=Dojo Root",
        "verify shop.example at 2032-01-01: FAILED NotTimeValid",
        "match shop.example api.shop.example: no",
        "distrusted CN=Dojo Root",
        "verify shop.example: FAILED UntrustedRoot",
        "```",
        "",
        "The FAILED line lists the distinct `X509ChainStatusFlags` names, sorted. Those names are what you'll see inside real .NET errors such as `AuthenticationException: The remote certificate is invalid because of errors in the certificate chain: UntrustedRoot`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "match",
      "prompt": "Each `verify` setting mirrors part of `openssl verify -CAfile root.pem -untrusted int.pem -attime ... -purpose sslserver leaf.pem`. Match them.",
      "pairs": [
        [
          "`-CAfile root.pem`",
          "`CustomTrustStore.Add(root)` with `CustomRootTrust`"
        ],
        [
          "`-untrusted int.pem`",
          "`ExtraStore.Add(intermediate)`"
        ],
        [
          "`-attime`",
          "`VerificationTime`"
        ],
        [
          "`-purpose sslserver`",
          "`ApplicationPolicy.Add(new Oid(\"1.3.6.1.5.5.7.3.1\"))`"
        ],
        [
          "(no network lookups)",
          "`DisableCertificateDownloads = true`"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "mcq",
      "prompt": "`distrust Dojo Root` keeps the root in `ExtraStore` instead of dropping it entirely. Why does that change the error from `PartialChain` to `UntrustedRoot`?",
      "options": [
        "The builder can now reach the root, so the chain is complete but ends at a root nobody trusts",
        "ExtraStore certificates are trusted at a lower level",
        "UntrustedRoot is always reported when CustomTrustStore is empty",
        "PartialChain only happens on Linux"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "explain": "`PartialChain`: the builder could not find an issuer. `UntrustedRoot`: it found the whole path, up to a self-signed root that is not a trust anchor. Same pair as openssl errors 20 and 19."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "A leaf valid 2030-01-01 to 2031-01-01, verified in 2032. What does this print?",
      "code": [
        "using System.Security.Cryptography;",
        "using System.Security.Cryptography.X509Certificates;",
        "var root = DojoCert(\"CN=Dojo Root\", null, true, naYear: 2050);",
        "var leaf = DojoCert(\"CN=shop.example\", root, false, \"shop.example\", nbYear: 2030, naYear: 2031);",
        "using var chain = new X509Chain();",
        "chain.ChainPolicy.TrustMode = X509ChainTrustMode.CustomRootTrust;",
        "chain.ChainPolicy.CustomTrustStore.Add(root);",
        "chain.ChainPolicy.RevocationMode = X509RevocationMode.NoCheck;",
        "chain.ChainPolicy.VerificationTime = new DateTime(2032, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc);",
        "Console.WriteLine(chain.Build(leaf));",
        "Console.WriteLine(string.Join(\", \", chain.ChainStatus.Select(s => s.Status).Distinct()));",
        "Console.WriteLine(leaf.MatchesHostname(\"www.shop.example\", allowCommonName: false));",
        "static X509Certificate2 DojoCert(string subject, X509Certificate2? issuer, bool isCa, string? dns = null, string? eku = null, int nbYear = 2030, int naYear = 2035)",
        "{",
        "    var key = ECDsa.Create(ECCurve.NamedCurves.nistP256);",
        "    var req = new CertificateRequest(subject, key, HashAlgorithmName.SHA256);",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509BasicConstraintsExtension(isCa, false, 0, true));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509KeyUsageExtension(isCa ? X509KeyUsageFlags.KeyCertSign | X509KeyUsageFlags.CrlSign : X509KeyUsageFlags.DigitalSignature, true));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509SubjectKeyIdentifierExtension(req.PublicKey, false));",
        "    if (dns != null) { var b = new SubjectAlternativeNameBuilder(); foreach (var d in dns.Split(',')) b.AddDnsName(d); req.CertificateExtensions.Add(b.Build()); }",
        "    if (eku != null) req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509EnhancedKeyUsageExtension(new OidCollection { new Oid(eku) }, false));",
        "    var nb = new DateTimeOffset(nbYear, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero);",
        "    var na = new DateTimeOffset(naYear, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero);",
        "    if (issuer == null) return req.CreateSelfSigned(nb, na);",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(X509AuthorityKeyIdentifierExtension.CreateFromCertificate(issuer, true, false));",
        "    var serial = RandomNumberGenerator.GetBytes(8); serial[0] &= 0x7F;",
        "    using var pub = req.Create(issuer, nb, na, serial);",
        "    return pub.CopyWithPrivateKey(key);",
        "}"
      ],
      "answer": [
        "False",
        "NotTimeValid",
        "False"
      ],
      "explain": "Expired shows as `NotTimeValid`. The SAN holds only `shop.example`, so `www.shop.example` does not match."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "mode": "write",
      "title": "mini-ca: verify, distrust, match",
      "prompt": [
        "Extend mini-ca with `verify`, `distrust` and `match`.",
        "",
        "**verify NAME [at YYYY-MM-DD]**: build an `X509Chain` for NAME:",
        "",
        "- `CustomRootTrust`; every root not distrusted goes in `CustomTrustStore`; every other certificate except the target goes in `ExtraStore`",
        "- `RevocationMode = NoCheck`, `DisableCertificateDownloads = true`, `VerificationTime` = the date at 00:00 UTC (default 2030-06-01)",
        "- for leaves, `ApplicationPolicy` serverAuth",
        "- no problems: `verify ARG: OK` then each chain element's subject indented two spaces, leaf first",
        "- otherwise: `verify ARG: FAILED ` + distinct non-`NoError` status names, sorted ordinally, comma-separated",
        "- `ARG` is the text after `verify` exactly as typed. A bad date: `error: dates look like 2030-06-01`",
        "",
        "**distrust ROOTNAME**: prints `distrusted CN=ROOTNAME`; not a root: `error: 'NAME' is not a root`.",
        "",
        "**match NAME HOST**: `match NAME HOST: yes` or `no` (SAN only, wildcards allowed, no CN fallback). Missing host: `error: match needs a name and a host`.",
        "",
        "```text",
        "> root Dojo Root",
        "> intermediate Issuing CA",
        "> issue shop.example www.shop.example",
        "> verify shop.example",
        "> verify shop.example at 2032-01-01",
        "> match shop.example api.shop.example",
        "> distrust Dojo Root",
        "> verify shop.example",
        "created root CN=Dojo Root (2030-01-01 to 2050-01-01)",
        "created intermediate CN=Issuing CA under CN=Dojo Root (2030-01-01 to 2040-01-01)",
        "issued CN=shop.example by CN=Issuing CA (2030-01-01 to 2031-01-01) for shop.example, www.shop.example",
        "verify shop.example: OK",
        "  CN=shop.example",
        "  CN=Issuing CA",
        "  CN=Dojo Root",
        "verify shop.example at 2032-01-01: FAILED NotTimeValid",
        "match shop.example api.shop.example: no",
        "distrusted CN=Dojo Root",
        "verify shop.example: FAILED UntrustedRoot",
        "```",
        "",
        "Names contain spaces, so split `match` on the **last** space and `verify` on `\" at \"`."
      ],
      "starter": [
        "using System.Security.Cryptography;",
        "using System.Security.Cryptography.X509Certificates;",
        "",
        "var certs = new Dictionary<string, Entry>();",
        "var order = new List<string>();",
        "int serials = 0;",
        "Entry? currentRoot = null;",
        "Entry? currentInter = null;",
        "",
        "string? line;",
        "while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) != null)",
        "{",
        "    line = line.Trim();",
        "    if (line.Length == 0 || line.StartsWith(\"#\")) continue;",
        "    int space = line.IndexOf(' ');",
        "    string cmd = space < 0 ? line : line[..space];",
        "    string arg = space < 0 ? \"\" : line[(space + 1)..].Trim();",
        "    switch (cmd)",
        "    {",
        "        case \"root\":",
        "        {",
        "            if (arg == \"\") { Console.WriteLine(\"error: root needs a name\"); break; }",
        "            if (certs.ContainsKey(arg)) { Console.WriteLine($\"error: '{arg}' already exists\"); break; }",
        "           var made = currentRoot = Add(MakeRoot(arg));",
        "            Console.WriteLine($\"created root {made.Cert.Subject} ({Dates(made.Cert)})\");",
        "            break;",
        "        }",
        "       case \"intermediate\":",
        "       {",
        "           if (arg == \"\") { Console.WriteLine(\"error: intermediate needs a name\"); break; }",
        "           if (certs.ContainsKey(arg)) { Console.WriteLine($\"error: '{arg}' already exists\"); break; }",
        "           if (currentRoot == null) { Console.WriteLine(\"error: no root yet\"); break; }",
        "           var made = currentInter = Add(MakeIntermediate(arg, currentRoot));",
        "           Console.WriteLine($\"created intermediate {made.Cert.Subject} under {currentRoot.Cert.Subject} ({Dates(made.Cert)})\");",
        "           break;",
        "       }",
        "       case \"issue\":",
        "       {",
        "           var hosts = arg.Split(' ', StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries);",
        "           if (hosts.Length == 0) { Console.WriteLine(\"error: issue needs at least one host\"); break; }",
        "           if (certs.ContainsKey(hosts[0])) { Console.WriteLine($\"error: '{hosts[0]}' already exists\"); break; }",
        "           if (currentInter == null) { Console.WriteLine(\"error: no intermediate yet\"); break; }",
        "           var made = Add(MakeLeaf(hosts, currentInter));",
        "           Console.WriteLine($\"issued {made.Cert.Subject} by {currentInter.Cert.Subject} ({Dates(made.Cert)}) for {string.Join(\", \", hosts)}\");",
        "           break;",
        "       }",
        "        case \"show\":",
        "        {",
        "            var found = Find(arg);",
        "            if (found != null) Show(found);",
        "            break;",
        "        }",
        "        case \"list\":",
        "        {",
        "            foreach (var name in order)",
        "            {",
        "                var x = certs[name];",
        "                Console.WriteLine(x.Parent == null ? $\"{x.Kind} {x.Cert.Subject}\" : $\"{x.Kind} {x.Cert.Subject} (issued by {x.Parent.Cert.Subject})\");",
        "            }",
        "            break;",
        "        }",
        "        default:",
        "            Console.WriteLine($\"error: unknown command '{cmd}'\");",
        "            break;",
        "    }",
        "}",
        "",
        "Entry Add(Entry entry)",
        "{",
        "    certs[entry.Name] = entry;",
        "    order.Add(entry.Name);",
        "    return entry;",
        "}",
        "",
        "Entry? Find(string name)",
        "{",
        "    if (certs.TryGetValue(name, out var found)) return found;",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"error: no certificate named '{name}'\");",
        "    return null;",
        "}",
        "",
        "byte[] Serial() => new byte[] { 0x01, (byte)++serials };",
        "",
        "Entry MakeRoot(string name)",
        "{",
        "    var key = ECDsa.Create(ECCurve.NamedCurves.nistP256);",
        "    var req = new CertificateRequest(\"CN=\" + name, key, HashAlgorithmName.SHA256);",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509BasicConstraintsExtension(true, false, 0, true));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509KeyUsageExtension(X509KeyUsageFlags.KeyCertSign | X509KeyUsageFlags.CrlSign, true));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509SubjectKeyIdentifierExtension(req.PublicKey, false));",
        "    return new Entry(name, \"root\", req.CreateSelfSigned(Day(2030), Day(2050)), null);",
        "}",
        "",
        "Entry MakeIntermediate(string name, Entry parent)",
        "{",
        "    var key = ECDsa.Create(ECCurve.NamedCurves.nistP256);",
        "    var req = new CertificateRequest(\"CN=\" + name, key, HashAlgorithmName.SHA256);",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509BasicConstraintsExtension(true, true, 0, true));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509KeyUsageExtension(X509KeyUsageFlags.KeyCertSign | X509KeyUsageFlags.CrlSign, true));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509SubjectKeyIdentifierExtension(req.PublicKey, false));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(X509AuthorityKeyIdentifierExtension.CreateFromCertificate(parent.Cert, true, false));",
        "    using var pub = req.Create(parent.Cert, Day(2030), Day(2040), Serial());",
        "    return new Entry(name, \"intermediate\", pub.CopyWithPrivateKey(key), parent);",
        "}",
        "",
        "Entry MakeLeaf(string[] hosts, Entry parent)",
        "{",
        "    var key = ECDsa.Create(ECCurve.NamedCurves.nistP256);",
        "    var req = new CertificateRequest(\"CN=\" + hosts[0], key, HashAlgorithmName.SHA256);",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509BasicConstraintsExtension(false, false, 0, true));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509KeyUsageExtension(X509KeyUsageFlags.DigitalSignature, true));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509EnhancedKeyUsageExtension(new OidCollection { new Oid(\"1.3.6.1.5.5.7.3.1\") }, false));",
        "    var san = new SubjectAlternativeNameBuilder();",
        "    foreach (var h in hosts) san.AddDnsName(h);",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(san.Build());",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509SubjectKeyIdentifierExtension(req.PublicKey, false));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(X509AuthorityKeyIdentifierExtension.CreateFromCertificate(parent.Cert, true, false));",
        "    using var pub = req.Create(parent.Cert, Day(2030), Day(2031), Serial());",
        "    return new Entry(hosts[0], \"leaf\", pub.CopyWithPrivateKey(key), parent);",
        "}",
        "",
        "void Show(Entry entry)",
        "{",
        "    var c = entry.Cert;",
        "    Console.WriteLine(c.Subject);",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"  issuer: {c.Issuer}\");",
        "    var bc = c.Extensions.OfType<X509BasicConstraintsExtension>().FirstOrDefault();",
        "   string ca = bc == null || !bc.CertificateAuthority ? \"no\"",
        "       : bc.HasPathLengthConstraint ? $\"yes, pathlen {bc.PathLengthConstraint}\" : \"yes, no pathlen limit\";",
        "   Console.WriteLine($\"  ca: {ca}\");",
        "   var san = c.Extensions.OfType<X509SubjectAlternativeNameExtension>().FirstOrDefault();",
        "   if (san != null) Console.WriteLine($\"  san: {string.Join(\", \", san.EnumerateDnsNames())}\");",
        "   var eku = c.Extensions.OfType<X509EnhancedKeyUsageExtension>().FirstOrDefault();",
        "   if (eku != null) Console.WriteLine($\"  eku: {string.Join(\", \", eku.EnhancedKeyUsages.Cast<Oid>().Select(o => EkuName(o.Value)))}\");",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"  valid: {Dates(c)}\");",
        "}",
        "",
        "static DateTimeOffset Day(int year) => new DateTimeOffset(year, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero);",
        "static string Ymd(DateTime t) => t.ToUniversalTime().ToString(\"yyyy-MM-dd\");",
        "static string Dates(X509Certificate2 c) => $\"{Ymd(c.NotBefore)} to {Ymd(c.NotAfter)}\";",
        "static string EkuName(string? oid) => oid switch",
        "{",
        "    \"1.3.6.1.5.5.7.3.1\" => \"serverAuth\",",
        "    \"1.3.6.1.5.5.7.3.2\" => \"clientAuth\",",
        "    _ => oid ?? \"unknown\"",
        "};",
        "",
        "record Entry(string Name, string Kind, X509Certificate2 Cert, Entry? Parent);"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "using System.Security.Cryptography;",
        "using System.Security.Cryptography.X509Certificates;",
        "using System.Globalization;",
        "",
        "var certs = new Dictionary<string, Entry>();",
        "var order = new List<string>();",
        "int serials = 0;",
        "Entry? currentRoot = null;",
        "Entry? currentInter = null;",
        "var distrusted = new HashSet<string>();",
        "",
        "string? line;",
        "while ((line = Console.ReadLine()) != null)",
        "{",
        "    line = line.Trim();",
        "    if (line.Length == 0 || line.StartsWith(\"#\")) continue;",
        "    int space = line.IndexOf(' ');",
        "    string cmd = space < 0 ? line : line[..space];",
        "    string arg = space < 0 ? \"\" : line[(space + 1)..].Trim();",
        "    switch (cmd)",
        "    {",
        "        case \"root\":",
        "        {",
        "            if (arg == \"\") { Console.WriteLine(\"error: root needs a name\"); break; }",
        "            if (certs.ContainsKey(arg)) { Console.WriteLine($\"error: '{arg}' already exists\"); break; }",
        "           var made = currentRoot = Add(MakeRoot(arg));",
        "            Console.WriteLine($\"created root {made.Cert.Subject} ({Dates(made.Cert)})\");",
        "            break;",
        "        }",
        "       case \"intermediate\":",
        "       {",
        "           if (arg == \"\") { Console.WriteLine(\"error: intermediate needs a name\"); break; }",
        "           if (certs.ContainsKey(arg)) { Console.WriteLine($\"error: '{arg}' already exists\"); break; }",
        "           if (currentRoot == null) { Console.WriteLine(\"error: no root yet\"); break; }",
        "           var made = currentInter = Add(MakeIntermediate(arg, currentRoot));",
        "           Console.WriteLine($\"created intermediate {made.Cert.Subject} under {currentRoot.Cert.Subject} ({Dates(made.Cert)})\");",
        "           break;",
        "       }",
        "       case \"issue\":",
        "       {",
        "           var hosts = arg.Split(' ', StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries);",
        "           if (hosts.Length == 0) { Console.WriteLine(\"error: issue needs at least one host\"); break; }",
        "           if (certs.ContainsKey(hosts[0])) { Console.WriteLine($\"error: '{hosts[0]}' already exists\"); break; }",
        "           if (currentInter == null) { Console.WriteLine(\"error: no intermediate yet\"); break; }",
        "           var made = Add(MakeLeaf(hosts, currentInter));",
        "           Console.WriteLine($\"issued {made.Cert.Subject} by {currentInter.Cert.Subject} ({Dates(made.Cert)}) for {string.Join(\", \", hosts)}\");",
        "           break;",
        "       }",
        "        case \"show\":",
        "        {",
        "            var found = Find(arg);",
        "            if (found != null) Show(found);",
        "            break;",
        "        }",
        "        case \"list\":",
        "        {",
        "            foreach (var name in order)",
        "            {",
        "                var x = certs[name];",
        "                Console.WriteLine(x.Parent == null ? $\"{x.Kind} {x.Cert.Subject}\" : $\"{x.Kind} {x.Cert.Subject} (issued by {x.Parent.Cert.Subject})\");",
        "            }",
        "            break;",
        "        }",
        "       case \"distrust\":",
        "       {",
        "           var found = Find(arg);",
        "           if (found == null) break;",
        "           if (found.Kind != \"root\") { Console.WriteLine($\"error: '{arg}' is not a root\"); break; }",
        "           distrusted.Add(found.Name);",
        "           Console.WriteLine($\"distrusted {found.Cert.Subject}\");",
        "           break;",
        "       }",
        "       case \"match\":",
        "       {",
        "           int last = arg.LastIndexOf(' ');",
        "           if (last < 0) { Console.WriteLine(\"error: match needs a name and a host\"); break; }",
        "           var found = Find(arg[..last]);",
        "           if (found == null) break;",
        "           string host = arg[(last + 1)..];",
        "           bool ok = found.Cert.MatchesHostname(host, allowWildcards: true, allowCommonName: false);",
        "           Console.WriteLine($\"match {found.Name} {host}: {(ok ? \"yes\" : \"no\")}\");",
        "           break;",
        "       }",
        "       case \"verify\":",
        "       {",
        "           string name = arg;",
        "           var at = new DateTime(2030, 6, 1, 0, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc);",
        "           int atPos = arg.IndexOf(\" at \");",
        "           if (atPos >= 0)",
        "           {",
        "               name = arg[..atPos];",
        "               if (!DateTime.TryParseExact(arg[(atPos + 4)..].Trim(), \"yyyy-MM-dd\", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture,",
        "                       DateTimeStyles.AssumeUniversal | DateTimeStyles.AdjustToUniversal, out at))",
        "               { Console.WriteLine(\"error: dates look like 2030-06-01\"); break; }",
        "           }",
        "           var found = Find(name);",
        "           if (found != null) Verify(found, at, arg);",
        "           break;",
        "       }",
        "        default:",
        "            Console.WriteLine($\"error: unknown command '{cmd}'\");",
        "            break;",
        "    }",
        "}",
        "",
        "Entry Add(Entry entry)",
        "{",
        "    certs[entry.Name] = entry;",
        "    order.Add(entry.Name);",
        "    return entry;",
        "}",
        "",
        "Entry? Find(string name)",
        "{",
        "    if (certs.TryGetValue(name, out var found)) return found;",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"error: no certificate named '{name}'\");",
        "    return null;",
        "}",
        "",
        "byte[] Serial() => new byte[] { 0x01, (byte)++serials };",
        "",
        "Entry MakeRoot(string name)",
        "{",
        "    var key = ECDsa.Create(ECCurve.NamedCurves.nistP256);",
        "    var req = new CertificateRequest(\"CN=\" + name, key, HashAlgorithmName.SHA256);",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509BasicConstraintsExtension(true, false, 0, true));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509KeyUsageExtension(X509KeyUsageFlags.KeyCertSign | X509KeyUsageFlags.CrlSign, true));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509SubjectKeyIdentifierExtension(req.PublicKey, false));",
        "    return new Entry(name, \"root\", req.CreateSelfSigned(Day(2030), Day(2050)), null);",
        "}",
        "",
        "Entry MakeIntermediate(string name, Entry parent)",
        "{",
        "    var key = ECDsa.Create(ECCurve.NamedCurves.nistP256);",
        "    var req = new CertificateRequest(\"CN=\" + name, key, HashAlgorithmName.SHA256);",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509BasicConstraintsExtension(true, true, 0, true));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509KeyUsageExtension(X509KeyUsageFlags.KeyCertSign | X509KeyUsageFlags.CrlSign, true));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509SubjectKeyIdentifierExtension(req.PublicKey, false));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(X509AuthorityKeyIdentifierExtension.CreateFromCertificate(parent.Cert, true, false));",
        "    using var pub = req.Create(parent.Cert, Day(2030), Day(2040), Serial());",
        "    return new Entry(name, \"intermediate\", pub.CopyWithPrivateKey(key), parent);",
        "}",
        "",
        "Entry MakeLeaf(string[] hosts, Entry parent)",
        "{",
        "    var key = ECDsa.Create(ECCurve.NamedCurves.nistP256);",
        "    var req = new CertificateRequest(\"CN=\" + hosts[0], key, HashAlgorithmName.SHA256);",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509BasicConstraintsExtension(false, false, 0, true));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509KeyUsageExtension(X509KeyUsageFlags.DigitalSignature, true));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509EnhancedKeyUsageExtension(new OidCollection { new Oid(\"1.3.6.1.5.5.7.3.1\") }, false));",
        "    var san = new SubjectAlternativeNameBuilder();",
        "    foreach (var h in hosts) san.AddDnsName(h);",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(san.Build());",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(new X509SubjectKeyIdentifierExtension(req.PublicKey, false));",
        "    req.CertificateExtensions.Add(X509AuthorityKeyIdentifierExtension.CreateFromCertificate(parent.Cert, true, false));",
        "    using var pub = req.Create(parent.Cert, Day(2030), Day(2031), Serial());",
        "    return new Entry(hosts[0], \"leaf\", pub.CopyWithPrivateKey(key), parent);",
        "}",
        "",
        "void Show(Entry entry)",
        "{",
        "    var c = entry.Cert;",
        "    Console.WriteLine(c.Subject);",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"  issuer: {c.Issuer}\");",
        "    var bc = c.Extensions.OfType<X509BasicConstraintsExtension>().FirstOrDefault();",
        "   string ca = bc == null || !bc.CertificateAuthority ? \"no\"",
        "       : bc.HasPathLengthConstraint ? $\"yes, pathlen {bc.PathLengthConstraint}\" : \"yes, no pathlen limit\";",
        "   Console.WriteLine($\"  ca: {ca}\");",
        "   var san = c.Extensions.OfType<X509SubjectAlternativeNameExtension>().FirstOrDefault();",
        "   if (san != null) Console.WriteLine($\"  san: {string.Join(\", \", san.EnumerateDnsNames())}\");",
        "   var eku = c.Extensions.OfType<X509EnhancedKeyUsageExtension>().FirstOrDefault();",
        "   if (eku != null) Console.WriteLine($\"  eku: {string.Join(\", \", eku.EnhancedKeyUsages.Cast<Oid>().Select(o => EkuName(o.Value)))}\");",
        "    Console.WriteLine($\"  valid: {Dates(c)}\");",
        "}",
        "",
        "void Verify(Entry target, DateTime at, string label)",
        "{",
        "    using var chain = new X509Chain();",
        "    chain.ChainPolicy.TrustMode = X509ChainTrustMode.CustomRootTrust;",
        "    chain.ChainPolicy.RevocationMode = X509RevocationMode.NoCheck;",
        "    chain.ChainPolicy.DisableCertificateDownloads = true;",
        "    chain.ChainPolicy.VerificationTime = at;",
        "    foreach (var x in certs.Values)",
        "    {",
        "        if (x.Kind == \"root\" && !distrusted.Contains(x.Name)) chain.ChainPolicy.CustomTrustStore.Add(x.Cert);",
        "        else if (x != target) chain.ChainPolicy.ExtraStore.Add(x.Cert);",
        "    }",
        "    if (target.Kind == \"leaf\") chain.ChainPolicy.ApplicationPolicy.Add(new Oid(\"1.3.6.1.5.5.7.3.1\"));",
        "    chain.Build(target.Cert);",
        "    var problems = chain.ChainStatus.Select(s => s.Status).Where(s => s != X509ChainStatusFlags.NoError)",
        "        .Distinct().Select(s => s.ToString()).ToList();",
        "    problems.Sort(StringComparer.Ordinal);",
        "    if (problems.Count == 0)",
        "    {",
        "        Console.WriteLine($\"verify {label}: OK\");",
        "        foreach (var el in chain.ChainElements) Console.WriteLine($\"  {el.Certificate.Subject}\");",
        "    }",
        "    else",
        "    {",
        "        Console.WriteLine($\"verify {label}: FAILED {string.Join(\", \", problems)}\");",
        "    }",
        "}",
        "",
        "static DateTimeOffset Day(int year) => new DateTimeOffset(year, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero);",
        "static string Ymd(DateTime t) => t.ToUniversalTime().ToString(\"yyyy-MM-dd\");",
        "static string Dates(X509Certificate2 c) => $\"{Ymd(c.NotBefore)} to {Ymd(c.NotAfter)}\";",
        "static string EkuName(string? oid) => oid switch",
        "{",
        "    \"1.3.6.1.5.5.7.3.1\" => \"serverAuth\",",
        "    \"1.3.6.1.5.5.7.3.2\" => \"clientAuth\",",
        "    _ => oid ?? \"unknown\"",
        "};",
        "",
        "record Entry(string Name, string Kind, X509Certificate2 Cert, Entry? Parent);"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "`DateTime.TryParseExact(text, \"yyyy-MM-dd\", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, DateTimeStyles.AssumeUniversal | DateTimeStyles.AdjustToUniversal, out at)` (add `using System.Globalization;`).",
        "Problems: `chain.ChainStatus.Select(s => s.Status).Where(s => s != X509ChainStatusFlags.NoError).Distinct().Select(s => s.ToString()).ToList()`, then `Sort(StringComparer.Ordinal)`.",
        "`found.Cert.MatchesHostname(host, allowWildcards: true, allowCommonName: false)`"
      ],
      "carry": true,
      "tests": [
        {
          "name": "verifies a good chain",
          "stdin": [
            "root Dojo Root",
            "intermediate Issuing CA",
            "issue shop.example www.shop.example",
            "verify shop.example",
            "verify Issuing CA",
            "verify Dojo Root"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "created root CN=Dojo Root (2030-01-01 to 2050-01-01)",
            "created intermediate CN=Issuing CA under CN=Dojo Root (2030-01-01 to 2040-01-01)",
            "issued CN=shop.example by CN=Issuing CA (2030-01-01 to 2031-01-01) for shop.example, www.shop.example",
            "verify shop.example: OK",
            "  CN=shop.example",
            "  CN=Issuing CA",
            "  CN=Dojo Root",
            "verify Issuing CA: OK",
            "  CN=Issuing CA",
            "  CN=Dojo Root",
            "verify Dojo Root: OK",
            "  CN=Dojo Root"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "reports an expired leaf",
          "stdin": [
            "root Dojo Root",
            "intermediate Issuing CA",
            "issue shop.example",
            "verify shop.example at 2032-01-01",
            "verify shop.example at 2030-12-31",
            "verify shop.example at soon"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "created root CN=Dojo Root (2030-01-01 to 2050-01-01)",
            "created intermediate CN=Issuing CA under CN=Dojo Root (2030-01-01 to 2040-01-01)",
            "issued CN=shop.example by CN=Issuing CA (2030-01-01 to 2031-01-01) for shop.example",
            "verify shop.example at 2032-01-01: FAILED NotTimeValid",
            "verify shop.example at 2030-12-31: OK",
            "  CN=shop.example",
            "  CN=Issuing CA",
            "  CN=Dojo Root",
            "error: dates look like 2030-06-01"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "reports an untrusted root",
          "stdin": [
            "root Dojo Root",
            "intermediate Issuing CA",
            "issue shop.example",
            "distrust Dojo Root",
            "verify shop.example",
            "distrust shop.example"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "created root CN=Dojo Root (2030-01-01 to 2050-01-01)",
            "created intermediate CN=Issuing CA under CN=Dojo Root (2030-01-01 to 2040-01-01)",
            "issued CN=shop.example by CN=Issuing CA (2030-01-01 to 2031-01-01) for shop.example",
            "distrusted CN=Dojo Root",
            "verify shop.example: FAILED UntrustedRoot",
            "error: 'shop.example' is not a root"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "checks host names against the SAN",
          "stdin": [
            "root Dojo Root",
            "intermediate Issuing CA",
            "issue shop.example www.shop.example",
            "match shop.example www.shop.example",
            "match shop.example api.shop.example",
            "match shop.example"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "created root CN=Dojo Root (2030-01-01 to 2050-01-01)",
            "created intermediate CN=Issuing CA under CN=Dojo Root (2030-01-01 to 2040-01-01)",
            "issued CN=shop.example by CN=Issuing CA (2030-01-01 to 2031-01-01) for shop.example, www.shop.example",
            "match shop.example www.shop.example: yes",
            "match shop.example api.shop.example: no",
            "error: match needs a name and a host"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "earlier commands still work",
          "stdin": [
            "root Dojo Root",
            "intermediate Issuing CA",
            "issue shop.example",
            "list",
            "show Issuing CA"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "created root CN=Dojo Root (2030-01-01 to 2050-01-01)",
            "created intermediate CN=Issuing CA under CN=Dojo Root (2030-01-01 to 2040-01-01)",
            "issued CN=shop.example by CN=Issuing CA (2030-01-01 to 2031-01-01) for shop.example",
            "root CN=Dojo Root",
            "intermediate CN=Issuing CA (issued by CN=Dojo Root)",
            "leaf CN=shop.example (issued by CN=Issuing CA)",
            "CN=Issuing CA",
            "  issuer: CN=Dojo Root",
            "  ca: yes, pathlen 0",
            "  valid: 2030-01-01 to 2040-01-01"
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "still passes: issues a leaf with SANs",
          "stdin": [
            "root Dojo Root",
            "intermediate Issuing CA",
            "issue shop.example www.shop.example",
            "show shop.example"
          ],
          "expect": [
            "created root CN=Dojo Root (2030-01-01 to 2050-01-01)",
            "created intermediate CN=Issuing CA under CN=Dojo Root (2030-01-01 to 2040-01-01)",
            "issued CN=shop.example by CN=Issuing CA (2030-01-01 to 2031-01-01) for shop.example, www.shop.example",
            "CN=shop.example",
            "  issuer: CN=Issuing CA",
            "  ca: no",
            "  san: shop.example, www.shop.example",
            "  eku: serverAuth",
            "  valid: 2030-01-01 to 2031-01-01"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
